   "definition": "understand the role of neurotransmitters at synapses ",
   "video_id": "824333317"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "The Role of Neurotransmitters"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Neurones are not directly connected to each other\n- The tiny gap between two neurones is called a **synapse**\n- When an **electrical impulse** reaches the end of one neurone, it triggers the release of **neurotransmitters** (chemical messengers)\n- These **neurotransmitters** diffuse across the synapse and bind to the next neurone, causing a new electrical impulse to be generated\n- This process allows the **impulse to pass from one neurone to the next**"
  },
